> You can do it with {su'o}:
> {lo su'o re dacti}
> means "at least two things", which is pretty much the
> same as "things".

Or you could say {lo za'u dacti}. {za'u} defaults to {za'u pa},
"more than one". But I think more comon than {za'u} or {su'o re},
when plurality is made explicit, will be {so'u}, {so'o}, {so'i}, "a few",
"several", "many".

